.TH "XML2RESP" "1" "2026-11-07" "evalresp 5.0.1" "EarthScope programs"
.SH "NAME"
\fIxml2resp\fR \- convert a file from FDSN StationXML to SEED RESP format
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B xml2resp
[\fB\-v\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIoutput\fR]
[\fIinput\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fIxml2resp\fR reads one file in FDSN StationXML format and writes the
equivalent response information in RESP format, the legacy text format written
by \fIrdseed\fR.  It is intended to produce the same RESP as the IRIS\-WS package.
.LP
\fIevalresp\fR(1) reads StationXML directly, at the full precision of the file,
and does not need this program.  Use \fIxml2resp\fR to make RESP files for
software that reads only that format.  RESP carries fewer significant digits
than StationXML, so a response evaluated from the RESP file can differ slightly
from one evaluated from the StationXML.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
.BR \-o " " \fIfile\fR ", " \-\-output =\fIfile\fR
Write the RESP text to \fIfile\fR, which is overwritten.  The default is standard output.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose [=\fIlevel\fR]
Accepted, with an optional level that is a number attached to the option
(\fB\-v3\fR or \fB\-\-verbose=3\fR).  The option may be repeated as separate
words (\fB\-v \-v\fR); a level that is not a number, including the grouped form
\fB\-vv\fR, is rejected as invalid usage.  It does not change the messages
written: they are always written to standard error, as described under
\fBMESSAGES\fR.
.PP
\fIinput\fR is the StationXML file.  At most one may be given; if it is omitted,
the StationXML is read from standard input.
.SH "MESSAGES"
Each message is written to standard error with a date and a level, so it never
mixes with the RESP text on standard output.  The messages include the
files being read and written, and what stopped the conversion if it fails.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 on success.  Otherwise non\-zero, with a message on standard error:
1 for invalid usage, 2 for a memory error, 3 for a buffer error, 4 for input that
cannot be parsed as StationXML (including a RESP file), 5 for a file that cannot be
read or written, and 6 for a date that cannot be read.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
To convert a file:
.IP
xml2resp \-o RESP.IU.ANMO station.xml
.LP
To convert from standard input to standard output, and keep the messages in a file:
.IP
xml2resp < station.xml > RESP.IU.ANMO 2> messages.log
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fIevalresp\fR(1)
